ISSUE #8567: Potential NULL Pointer Dereference in MagickCore
Author: waugustus
Date: 2026-02-14T08:49:18Z
Labels: 
State: closed

[c0]
### ImageMagick version

7.1.2

### Operating system

Linux

### Operating system, version and so on

24.04

### Description

Hello ImageMagick maintainers,

While reviewing the source code of ImageMagick, we identified several potential NULL pointer dereference issues. To avoid wasting your time, we carefully analyzed the relevant execution paths and manually reviewed the affected code sections, and we believe these cases may be triggerable under certain conditions. We would greatly appreciate your feedback on whether they are considered valid.

Below are the details of each case.

## NPD 1: NULL Pointer Dereference in `MagickCore/transform.c TransformImage`

When `image->columns` or `image->rows` is 0 upon being passed to the `CloneImage` function, the function may return `NULL`.

```c
// ./MagickCore/image.c
MagickExport Image *CloneImage(const Image *image,const size_t columns,
  const size_t rows,const MagickBooleanType detach,ExceptionInfo *exception)
{
  double
    scale_x,
    scale_y;

  Image
    *clone_image;

  size_t
    length;

  /*
    Clone the image.
  */
  assert(image != (const Image *) NULL);
  assert(image->signature == MagickCoreSignature);
  assert(exception != (ExceptionInfo *) NULL);
  assert(exception->signature == MagickCoreSignature);
  if (IsEventLogging() != MagickFalse)
    (void) LogMagickEvent(TraceEvent,GetMagickModule(),"%s",image->filename);
  if ((image->columns == 0) || (image->rows == 0))
    {
      (void) ThrowMagickException(exception,GetMagickModule(),CorruptImageError,
        "NegativeOrZeroImageSize","`%s'",image->filename);
      return((Image *) NULL);
    }
   .....
```


In the `TransformImage` function, if `image->columns` or `image->rows` is 0, `CloneImage` may return `NULL`. The statement `transform_image = CloneImage(*image, 0, 0, MagickTrue, exception);` may therefore assign `NULL` to the `transform_image` variable. Subsequently, the condition`if ((transform_image->columns == geometry.width) && (transform_image->rows == geometry.height))` can trigger a null pointer dereference.

```c
// ./MagickCore/transform.c
MagickPrivate MagickBooleanType TransformImage(Image **image,
  const char *crop_geometry,const char *image_geometry,ExceptionInfo *exception)
{
  Image
    *resize_image,
    *transform_image;

  RectangleInfo
    geometry;

  assert(image != (Image **) NULL);
  assert((*image)->signature == MagickCoreSignature);
  if (IsEventLogging() != MagickFalse)
    (void) LogMagickEvent(TraceEvent,GetMagickModule(),"%s",(*image)->filename);
  transform_image=(*image);
  if (crop_geometry != (const char *) NULL)
    {
      Image
        *crop_image;

      /*
        Crop image to a user specified size.
      */
      crop_image=CropImageToTiles(*image,crop_geometry,exception);
      if (crop_image == (Image *) NULL)
        transform_image=CloneImage(*image,0,0,MagickTrue,exception);  // may return NULL
      else
        {
          transform_image=DestroyImage(transform_image);
          transform_image=GetFirstImageInList(crop_image);
        }
      *image=transform_image;
    }
  if (image_geometry == (const char *) NULL)
    return(MagickTrue);
  /*
    Scale image to a user specified size.
  */
  (void) ParseRegionGeometry(transform_image,image_geometry,&geometry,
    exception);
  if ((transform_image->columns == geometry.width) && //sink
      (transform_image->rows == geometry.height))
    return(MagickTrue);
  .....
}
```

## NPD 2: NULL Pointer Dereference in `CloseMagickLog`

When the `IsLogCacheInstantiated` function fails to create the log cache, `GetLogInfo` in `./MagickCore/log.c` may return `NULL`.

```c
// ./MagickCore/log.c
static LogInfo *GetLogInfo(const char *name,ExceptionInfo *exception)
{
  LogInfo
    *log_info;

  ElementInfo
    *p;

  assert(exception != (ExceptionInfo *) NULL);
  if (IsLogCacheInstantiated(exception) == MagickFalse)
    return((LogInfo *) NULL);
  ....

```

In the `CloseMagickLog` function, the `NULL` potentially returned by `GetLogInfo` is assigned to the `log_info` variable via`log_info = GetLogInfo("*", exception);` and is subsequently dereferenced in the statement`if (log_info->file != (FILE *) NULL)` causing a null pointer dereference.

```c
// ./MagickCore/log.c
MagickExport void CloseMagickLog(void)
{
  ExceptionInfo
    *exception;

  LogInfo
    *log_info;

  if (IsEventLogging() == MagickFalse)
    return;
  exception=AcquireExceptionInfo();
  log_info=GetLogInfo("*",exception);
  exception=DestroyExceptionInfo(exception);
  LockSemaphoreInfo(log_semaphore);
  if (log_info->file != (FILE *) NULL)
    {
      (void) FormatLocaleFile(log_info->file,"</log>\n");
      (void) fclose(log_info->file);
      log_info->file=(FILE *) NULL;
    }
  UnlockSemaphoreInfo(log_semaphore);
}
```

## NPD 3: NULL Pointer Dereference in `LogMagickEventList`

`GetLogInfo` can return `NULL` if the log system is not initialized or if memory allocation fails.  

```c
// ./MagickCore/log.c
static LogInfo *GetLogInfo(const char *name,ExceptionInfo *exception)
{
  LogInfo
    *log_info;

  ElementInfo
    *p;

  assert(exception != (ExceptionInfo *) NULL);
  if (IsLogCacheInstantiated(exception) == MagickFalse)
    return((LogInfo *) NULL);
  ....

```

In the `LogMagickEventList`, If `log_info` is `NULL`, accessing `log_info->event_semaphore` triggers a crash.

```c
// ./MagickCore/log.c
MagickExport MagickBooleanType LogMagickEventList(const LogEventType type,
  const char *module,const char *function,const size_t line,const char *format,
  va_list operands)
{
  char
    event[MagickPathExtent],
    *text;

  const char
    *domain;

  ExceptionInfo
    *exception;

  int
    n;

  LogInfo
    *log_info;

  exception=AcquireExceptionInfo();
  log_info=(LogInfo *) GetLogInfo("*",exception);
  exception=DestroyExceptionInfo(exception);
  if (log_info->event_semaphore == (SemaphoreInfo *) NULL)
    ActivateSemaphoreInfo(&log_info->event_semaphore);
  ...
}
```

## NPD 4: NULL Pointer Dereference in `SetLogMethod`

In the `GetValueFromLinkedList` function in `MagickCore/linked-list.c`, if `list_info->elements` is 0, the function may return `NULL`.

```c
// MagickCore/linked-list.c GetValueFromLinkedList
MagickExport void *GetValueFromLinkedList(LinkedListInfo *list_info,
  const size_t index)
{
  ElementInfo
    *next;

  ssize_t
    i;

  void
    *value;

  assert(list_info != (LinkedListInfo *) NULL);
  assert(list_info->signature == MagickCoreSignature);
  if (index >= list_info->elements)
    return((void *) NULL);
  ...
}
```


In `MagickCore/log.c` within the `SetLogMethod` function, a `NULL` potentially returned by `GetValueFromLinkedList` is assigned to the `log_info` variable, and is subsequently dereferenced in the statement `log_info->handler_mask = (LogHandlerType)(log_info->handler_mask | MethodHandler)`causing a null pointer dereference.

```c
// MagickCore/log.c SetLogMethod
MagickExport void SetLogMethod(MagickLogMethod method)
{
  ExceptionInfo
    *exception;

  LogInfo
    *log_info;

  exception=AcquireExceptionInfo();
  log_info=(LogInfo *) GetLogInfo("*",exception);
  exception=DestroyExceptionInfo(exception);
  LockSemaphoreInfo(log_semaphore);
  log_info=(LogInfo *) GetValueFromLinkedList(log_cache,0);
  log_info->handler_mask=(LogHandlerType) (log_info->handler_mask |
    MethodHandler);
  log_info->method=method;
  UnlockSemaphoreInfo(log_semaphore);
}
```

## NPD 5: NULL Pointer Dereference in `GetPixelRed`

If `cache_info->storage_class` is `UndefinedClass`, `GetVirtualPixelsNexus` in `MagickCore/cache.c` may return `NULL`.

```c
// MagickCore/cache.c GetVirtualPixelsNexus
MagickPrivate const Quantum *GetVirtualPixelsNexus(const Cache cache,
  NexusInfo *magick_restrict nexus_info)
{
  CacheInfo
    *magick_restrict cache_info;

  assert(cache != (Cache) NULL);
  cache_info=(CacheInfo *) cache;
  assert(cache_info->signature == MagickCoreSignature);
  if (cache_info->storage_class == UndefinedClass)
    return((Quantum *) NULL);
  return((const Quantum *) nexus_info->pixels);
}
```

If `cache_info->methods.get_virtual_pixels_handler` is `NULL` and `cache_info->storage_class` is `UndefinedClass`, the `GetVirtualPixelQueue` function may pass the `NULL` returned by `GetVirtualPixelsNexus` to its caller.

```c
// MagickCore/cache.c GetVirtualPixelQueue
MagickExport const Quantum *GetVirtualPixelQueue(const Image *image)
{
  CacheInfo
    *magick_restrict cache_info;

  const int
    id = GetOpenMPThreadId();

  assert(image != (const Image *) NULL);
  assert(image->signature == MagickCoreSignature);
  assert(image->cache != (Cache) NULL);
  cache_info=(CacheInfo *) image->cache;
  assert(cache_info->signature == MagickCoreSignature);
  if (cache_info->methods.get_virtual_pixels_handler !=
       (GetVirtualPixelsHandler) NULL)
    return(cache_info->methods.get_virtual_pixels_handler(image));
  assert(id < (int) cache_info->number_threads);
  return(GetVirtualPixelsNexus(cache_info,cache_info->nexus_info[id]));
}
```

If `image->cache->methods.get_virtual_pixels_handler` is `NULL` and `image->cache->storage_class` is `UndefinedClass`, the `ExportQuantumPixels` function may assign a `NULL` returned by `GetVirtualPixelQueue` to the variable `p`. If the `quantum_type` variable is `CMYKAQuantum`, this `NULL` is then passed as a parameter to the `ExportCMYKAQuantum` function.

```c
// MagickCore/quantum-export.c ExportQuantumPixels

MagickExport size_t ExportQuantumPixels(const Image *image,
  CacheView *image_view,QuantumInfo *quantum_info,
  const QuantumType quantum_type,unsigned char *magick_restrict pixels,
  ExceptionInfo *exception)
{
  MagickSizeType
    number_pixels;

  const Quantum
    *magick_restrict p;

  size_t
    extent;

  ssize_t
    x;

  unsigned char
    *magick_restrict q;

  assert(image != (Image *) NULL);
  assert(image->signature == MagickCoreSignature);
  assert(quantum_info != (QuantumInfo *) NULL);
  assert(quantum_info->signature == MagickCoreSignature);
  assert(exception != (ExceptionInfo *) NULL);
  assert(exception->signature == MagickCoreSignature);
  if (IsEventLogging() != MagickFalse)
    (void) LogMagickEvent(TraceEvent,GetMagickModule(),"%s",image->filename);
  if (pixels == (unsigned char *) NULL)
    pixels=(unsigned char *) GetQuantumPixels(quantum_info);
  if (image_view == (CacheView *) NULL)
    {
      number_pixels=GetImageExtent(image);
      p=GetVirtualPixelQueue(image);
    }
  ...
  switch (quantum_type)
  {
    ...
    case CMYKAQuantum:
    {
      ExportCMYKAQuantum(image,quantum_info,number_pixels,p,q,exception);
      break;
    }
    ...
  }
  ...
}
```

In the `ExportCMYKAQuantum` function in `quantum-export.c`, the `NULL` carried by the variable `p` is passed to the `GetPixelRed` function.

```c
// quantum-export.c ExportCMYKAQuantum
static void ExportCMYKAQuantum(const Image *image,QuantumInfo *quantum_info,
  const MagickSizeType number_pixels,const Quantum *magick_restrict p,
  unsigned char *magick_restrict q,ExceptionInfo *exception)
{
  ssize_t
    x;

  if (image->colorspace != CMYKColorspace)
    {
      (void) ThrowMagickException(exception,GetMagickModule(),ImageError,
        "ColorSeparatedImageRequired","`%s'",image->filename);
      return;
    }
  switch (quantum_info->depth)
  {
    case 8:
    {
      unsigned char
        pixel;

      for (x=0; x < (ssize_t) number_pixels; x++)
      {
        pixel=ScaleQuantumToChar(GetPixelRed(image,p));
  ....
}

```

This results in a null pointer dereference in the `GetPixelRed` function.

```c
// pixel-accessor.h
static inline Quantum GetPixelRed(const Image *magick_restrict image,
  const Quantum *magick_restrict pixel)
{
  return(pixel[image->channel_map[RedPixelChannel].offset]);
}
```

## NPD 6: NULL Pointer Dereference in `NewXMLTreeTag`

If the `AcquireMagickMemory` function fails to allocate memory, it may return `NULL`; therefore, the `NewXMLTreeTag` function may also return `NULL`.

```c
// MagickCore/xml-tree.c NewXMLTreeTag
MagickExport XMLTreeInfo *NewXMLTreeTag(const char *tag)
{
  static const char
    *predefined_entities[NumberPredefinedEntities+1] =
    {
      "lt;", "&#60;", "gt;", "&#62;", "quot;", "&#34;",
      "apos;", "&#39;", "amp;", "&#38;", (char *) NULL
    };

  XMLTreeRoot
    *root;

  root=(XMLTreeRoot *) AcquireMagickMemory(sizeof(*root));
  if (root == (XMLTreeRoot *) NULL)
    return((XMLTreeInfo *) NULL);
  ...
}
```



In the `MagickCore/xml-tree.c` `NewXMLTree` function, the `NULL` pointer returned by `NewXMLTreeTag` is assigned to the `root` variable. Subsequently, when parsing the `DTD` format, this `NULL` pointer is passed into the `ParseInternalDoctype` function.

<img width="1555" height="1960" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a039fadb-b2cb-44ae-85b9-deeaac2225df" />

In the `MagickCore/xml-tree.c` `ParseInternalDoctype` function, a null pointer dereference may be triggered while parsing entity definitions.


<img width="1516" height="1687" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1d7e5e42-be6c-4c74-846e-8c9e7489339f" />

Additionally, in the `MagickCore/xml-tree.c` `NewXMLTree` function, processing XML data that begins with a letter or a `:` may also trigger a null pointer dereference.

<img width="1423" height="1556" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/278d991b-da5b-4508-9958-9b9f10939c4b" />


Additionally, when the parser reaches the logic for handling a self-closing tag, the `NULL` pointer may be passed to the `ParseCloseTag` function, where it can trigger a null pointer dereference.

<img width="1669" height="1877" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9744e0df-d6ea-41b2-8d42-0314fa633287" />
<img width="1264" height="439" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c8817b1e-2782-4456-9c57-7b308032230c" />

### Steps to Reproduce

At this stage, the issues were identified through careful manual code review and control-flow analysis. We have not yet constructed a working proof-of-concept input that reliably triggers the suspected NULL pointer dereference.

Based on the current analysis, the issue may become reachable under certain internal states (e.g., failed allocations or unexpected image properties), but additional guidance from maintainers may be needed to confirm reachability in practice.

If helpful, we are willing to assist with further analysis or provide additional details about the reasoning path.

### Images

At this time, we are unable to provide a specific image file that reproduces the issue, as no concrete triggering input has been constructed yet.

The report is based on source-level analysis of error-handling and NULL-check paths. If a triggering condition is confirmed, we will attempt to construct and provide a minimal reproducing input.


