ISSUE #8003: ImageMagick Incorrectly Handles Negative biHeight for Compressed Formats
Author: ElinorCoding
Date: 2025-03-03T06:30:01Z
Labels: 
State: closed

[c0]
### ImageMagick version

commit_hash=`bc0bbec02` 

### Operating system

Linux

### Operating system, version and so on

### Platform - OS:  Ubuntu 22.04.05(ker:Linux6.10.11)  - Compiler: clang 14.0.0  - Architecture: x86_64

### Description



### Description  
Hi,  

I would like to report an observation regarding ImageMagick's handling of BMP files with compressed formats.

 According to the Microsoft documentation for the `BITMAPINFOHEADER` structure, the `biHeight` field **must be positive for compressed formats**, regardless of image orientation. However, I found that ImageMagick can still parse and process BMP files with negative `biHeight` values for compressed formats without any warnings or errors.  

This behavior might lead to inconsistencies when working with other tools or libraries that strictly adhere to the Microsoft specification.  

---

### Reference  
Microsoft Documentation: [BITMAPINFOHEADER structure](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/wingdi/ns-wingdi-bitmapinfoheader) section Members-`biHeight` 
Relevant Quote:  
> For compressed formats, **biHeight must be positive**, regardless of image orientation.  

---


### Steps to Reproduce


### Test Case  

I created a BMP file  with a compressed format and set the `biHeight` field to a negative value. ImageMagick was able to parse and process the file without any issues.  

![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a9c0e08f-d1b0-4a3a-b088-85e1fb73b69b)

you can see the biheight is `FFFFFFE0`,which means -32,and the compression is 1.
### reproduction:  
I test it both with the binary file in IM and the following code,and both do not report an error.
```bash
identify invalid_height_compress.bmp
```
```bash
convert invalid_height_compress.bmp test.bmp
```
Output:

![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3d17caf0-7957-44c8-8989-29341d8007dc)

Code
```C
#include <string>
#include <iostream>
#include <fstream>
#include <vector>
#include <cstdint>
#include <Magick++/Blob.h>
#include <Magick++/Image.h>
using namespace std;
using namespace Magick;

int main(int argc,char **argv) 
{ 
  // InitializeMagick(*argv);

  if (argc<2)
    {
        printf("need a bmp file\n");
        return 0;
    }

  Image image;
  try { 
    // Read a file
    image.read(argv[1] );
  } 
  catch( Exception &error_ ) 
    { 
      std::cout << "Caught exception: " << error_.what() << std::endl; 
      return 1; 
    } 
  return 0; 
}
```

- Expected Behavior
For BMP files with compressed formats, ImageMagick should:
1. Reject files with negative biHeight values.
2. Issue a warning or error indicating that the file does not comply with the Microsoft specification.

- Actual Behavior
ImageMagick successfully parses and processes BMP files with negative biHeight values for compressed formats, without any warnings or errors.





### Additional information
when I test it with graphicmagick, it reports an error with the following logic:
`Graphicmagick/coders/bmp.c: ReadBMPImage`

```c
    if ((bmp_info.height < 0) && (bmp_info.compression !=0))
        ThrowBMPReaderException(CorruptImageError,CompressionNotValid,image);
```
Hope this helps!



### Images

[testcase.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/19048608/testcase.zip)

---
Thank you for your attention to this issue!
Best regards,
Elinor

