ISSUE #7825: coders/meta.c Memory Leak
Author: youngjaechoi7
Date: 2024-12-07T14:08:29Z
Labels: 
State: closed

[c0]
### ImageMagick version

7.1.1-41

### Operating system

Linux

### Operating system, version and so on

Ubuntu 22.04.3 LTS 64bit

### Description

Hi, I found a memory leak vulnerability in imagemagick, Details are written at **Steps to Reproduce**.

### Steps to Reproduce

Located in coders/meta.c, 

In the `static ssize_t parse8BIMW(Image *ifile, Image *ofile)` function, memory is allocated to the `line` variable in the following code line. https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/blob/main/coders/meta.c#L653
```c  
line = (char *) AcquireQuantumMemory(inputlen,sizeof(*line));    //allocate a memory and assigned it to line
  if (line == (char *) NULL)
    return(-1);
  newstr = name = token = (char *) NULL;
  savedpos = 0;
  token_info=AcquireTokenInfo();
```

However, it can be seen that the allocated memory is not freed before returning, resulting a memory leak vulnerability.
https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/blob/main/coders/meta.c#L750
 ```c
                if (savedolen > 0)
                  {
                    MagickOffsetType
                      offset;

                    ssize_t diff = outputlen - savedolen;
                    currentpos = TellBlob(ofile);
                    if (currentpos < 0)
                      return(-1);    // return without free line pointed memory
                    offset=SeekBlob(ofile,savedpos,SEEK_SET);
                    if (offset < 0)
                      return(-1);    // return without free line pointed memory
                    (void) WriteBlobMSBLong(ofile,(unsigned int) diff);
                    offset=SeekBlob(ofile,currentpos,SEEK_SET);
                    if (offset < 0)
                      return(-1);
                    savedolen = 0L;
                  }
```

- A similar vulnerability was patched in `static ssize_t parse8BIM(Image *ifile, Image *ofile)` ([CVE-2018-14437](https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/issues/1190)), but it appears that the issue was not addressed in the `static ssize_t parse8BIMW(Image *ifile, Image *ofile)`  function.
https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/blob/main/coders/meta.c#L442
```c
if (currentpos < 0)
{
    line=DestroyString(line);
    return(-1);
}
```

### Images

![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e9b07979-0238-45fb-94ad-d58646bb0cf9)


--- COMMENTS ---
[c1] @dlemstra 2024-12-07T15:37:11Z:
Thanks for reporting this. And that was not the only leak. Other objects were also not properly freed. A patch for this was just pushed and this will be resolved in the next release.
---
[c2] @youngjaechoi7 2024-12-08T09:37:21Z:
Thank you for the quick response. I agree regarding the multiple memory leaks.

I'd like to point out that the `static ssize_t parse8BIM(Image ifile, Image ofile)` function also needs to be patched. Even though `static ssize_t parse8BIMW(Image ifile, Image ofile)` has been patched, memory leaks still persist in the `parse8BIM` function.

Specifically, to prevent memory leaks, other allocations (token, newstr, name) need to be freed properly, rather than only freeing 'line' before returning. Just like in parse8BMW.
https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/blob/main/coders/meta.c#L442
https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/blob/main/coders/meta.c#L756

@dlemstra Will these issues be assigned CVE IDs?

Credit: Youngjae Choi, Seunghoon Woo, Kyeongseok Yang, Sunha Park - Korea University
---
[c3] @dlemstra 2024-12-09T22:12:56Z:
Thanks for pointing out that we should also fix the possible memory leaks in that other method.

Right now we don't have a process or time to create those CVE's.
